&lt;li&gt;Participate in in-person events, off-sites, and community initiatives that reflect our mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build in-person relationships with team members and contribute to Nextdoor’s company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring To The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;15+ years of experience in digital media or advertising sales, with a consistent record of exceeding targets in high-growth environments, and/or the ability to perform at an advanced level in the domain&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of sales leadership experience, including managing managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record building and scaling regional or national sales teams from the ground up or through a period of significant growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep relationships across the Mid West brand and agency ecosystem&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic thinker who can connect customer needs to product solutions and translate that into a winning go-to-market plan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Executive presence and communication skills — comfortable in the boardroom with a CMO or on a whiteboard with your team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical orientation; you use data to diagnose problems, forecast accurately, and coach effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine passion for local community and belief in Nextdoor&#39;s mission&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eagerness to explore and apply AI and emerging technologies to reimagine how work gets done&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rewards&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Compensation, benefits, perks, and recognition programs at Nextdoor come together to create our total rewards package. Compensation will vary depending on your relevant skills, experience, and qualifications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The compensation range for this role includes a base salary + commission structure with a 60/40 split. Commission will vary depending on your achievement of sales-related goals and objectives. The budgeted OTE (on-target earnings) inclusive of base + commission is in the range of $320,000-$400,000 (base salary of $192,000-$240,000) on an annualized basis. The salary range will be determined by the candidate’s geographic location.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We expect to award a meaningful equity grant for this role. With quarterly vesting, your first vest date will take place within 3 months of your start date.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When it comes to benefits, we have you covered! Nextdoor employees can choose between a variety of health plans, including a 100% covered employee only plan option, and we also provide a OneMedical membership for concierge care.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nextdoor, we empower our employees to build stronger local communities. To create a platform where all feel welcome, we want our workforce to reflect the diversity of the neighbors we serve. We encourage everyone interested in our mission to apply. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, gender, religion, sexual orientation, age, or any other trait that unfairly targets a group of people. In accordance with the San Francisco Fair Chance Ordinance, we always consider qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For information about our collection and use of applicants’ personal information, please see Nextdoor&#39;s Personnel Privacy Notice, found &lt;a href=&quot;https://help.nextdoor.com/s/article/Personnel-Privacy-Policy?language=en_US&quot;&gt;here&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;#Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nextdoor&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nextdoor (NYSE: NXDR) is the essential neighborhood network. Neighbors, public agencies, and businesses use Nextdoor to connect around local information that matters in more than 350,000 neighborhoods across 11 countries. Nextdoor builds innovative technology to foster local community, share important news, and create neighborhood connections at scale. Download the app and join the neighborhood at &lt;a href=&quot;http://nextdoor.com/&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;nextdoor.com&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Meet Your Future&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Neighbors&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Designer on Nextdoor&#39;s Consumer Product team, you&#39;ll help shape the future of how neighbors connect with one another, their neighborhoods, and local businesses and events. You&#39;ll join a collaborative team of designers, product managers, engineers, and researchers working to evolve and improve the experience across our platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re hiring a player-coach to lead craft for Consumer Design, someone who runs a rigorous crit, coaches designers toward their next level, and holds the line when speed and quality trade off, while still shipping hands-on work themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deeply human-centered and mission-driven, you&#39;re excited to create digital experiences that strengthen real-world connections and empower neighbors to build stronger communities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nextdoor, we operate in an AI-first environment and expect every team member to actively use AI tools as part of their workflow. We aren&#39;t looking for prompt engineers; we’re looking for people who use tools like Claude, Gemini, ChatGPT, and Glean to challenge their own thinking and take full ownership of AI-assisted outputs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We also offer a warm and inclusive work environment that embraces a hybrid employment model, blending an in office presence and work from home experience for our valued employees. The hiring team will go over these expectations with you if you are being considered for a role near one of our offices in San Francisco, Los Angeles, Chicago, Dallas, New York, and London.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; You’ll Make&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you excited by the challenge of raising the craft bar for a design team, coaching designers toward their next level, and still shipping hands-on work yourself? If so, this is the role for you. Please include a portfolio link along with your resume.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Running weekly design critiques and rebuilding a healthy manager-level review process so projects of every size get rigorous feedback at the right altitude&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishing regular 1:1s and growth plans for a team of consumer designers, and advocating for their growth and promotion during performance review cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the design capacity model across seven product areas, managing a team of 5 to 6 consumer designers. Owning the capacity model and the recommendation on where design headcount goes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Representing design&#39;s point of view in product discussions where speed and craft are in tension, starting with a key decision about how neighbors filter and navigate content in the app&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Arbitrating design-system exceptions, deciding when to say no to a one-off component that doesn&#39;t belong in our shared design system&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shipping hands-on design work yourself on at least one high-impact area of the consumer product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participating in in-person Nextdoor events such as trainings, off-sites, volunteer days, and team building exercises&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Building in-person relationships with team members and contributing to Nextdoor&#39;s company culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role reports directly to the EVP of Product and is the senior-most design voice in the Consumer org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring To The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in UX design, product design, or a related field, with a strong track record of designing and shipping user-centered products. Including experience directly managing designers through performance and promotion cycles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record as a player-coach,&amp;nbsp; practicing designer and people manager at once, with the discipline to protect your own IC time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calibrated craft judgment: you can run a crit, make a leveling call, and defend it in calibration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Figma and other design tools for creating wireframes, prototypes, and high-fidelity designs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with and contributing to design systems, ensuring consistency and scalability across surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of qualitative and quantitative research methods, with the ability to synthesize insights into actionable design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort holding a design position in rooms with executives, backed by evidence rather than taste&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with AI-assisted design tooling and a clear sense of where it helps and where it can&#39;t substitute for human judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us to design products that make a real-world impact, strengthening communities and bringing people closer together.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
